# Draneka Aquarium Breeder — Android v0.1 Adaptation Notes

## Purpose

This artifact derives an Android-specific client experience from the holistic Breeder v0.2 product model. It does not alter breeder domain ownership, cohort accounting, lineage semantics, or the Journal/Breeder shared-data boundary.

## Android decisions

1. **Breeder Home is the Android task root.** It has no in-app Back affordance. Android Back closes transient surfaces first and reaches an exit confirmation at the task root.
2. **Breeder Round is a focused full-screen operational flow.** Bottom navigation and the floating Quick Log action are suppressed while a round is active so accidental context switching is reduced.
3. **Routine round confirmations stay one-tap.** Consequential records use structured bottom sheets and inherit project/tank/cohort context.
4. **Photo Picker is preferred for existing media.** Broad storage permission is not modeled. Camera permission appears only when new capture is explicitly chosen.
5. **Notification permission is contextual.** It is associated with enabling breeder reminders instead of first launch.
6. **Offline writes remain explicit and queued.** The prototype shows retry/reconciliation rather than pretending local submission is already authoritative.
7. **Process restoration never auto-confirms a draft.** Recovered work remains visibly unsaved until the breeder continues and saves it.
8. **Unavailable context fails closed.** The client does not silently substitute another project, cohort, tank, or lineage record.
9. **Journal integration preserves event identity.** Shared feeding/care records appear with the same event identifier rather than being duplicated for Breeder and Journal.

## Holistic v0.2 boundary retained

Breeder Round remains hybrid: scheduled Today/Overdue work is included, then routine active breeder contexts are included where not already represented. This Android iteration intentionally does not adopt a new routine-frequency scheduling model.
